{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Young1961-T2-n150-W060-k3",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Synthesis of multiple antireflection films over a prescribed frequency band,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 51, 967-974 (1961). doi:10.1364/JOSA.51.000967 - Table II p. 973 (W = 0.60, n = 1.50, k = 3: n1 = 1.06186) and Eq. (30) n2 = sqrt(n), n3 = n/n1",
  "Notes": "Table II Tschebyscheff 3-layer AR coating from air to n = 1.50, W = 0.60.\nSpecification: Equiripple minimum of maximum reflection over W = 0.60.\nReported: Table I (k = 3, n = 1.50, W = 0.60): max amplitude reflection coefficient 0.01. Exact from Eq. (7): 0.0056 (R_max = 3.1e-5); R = 0 at band centre 550 nm for odd k. R = 0.04 (bare substrate) at 275 nm.\nNotes: As Young1961-T2-n150-W060-k2. n2 and n3 derived from Eq. (30), rounded to 5 decimals.\nLayers from Table II p. 973 (W = 0.60, n = 1.50, k = 3: n1 = 1.06186) and Eq. (30) n2 = sqrt(n), n3 = n/n1; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours max |r| 0.0056 from 423 to 786 nm; paper max |r| 0.01 (Table I).",
